  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZM-Nature Tourism Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal seeks to undertake analytical work to estimate the potential contribution of nature-based tourism to economic growth and poverty reduction in Zambia.  The Government has registered tourism as the third pillar for economic development (the other two being agriculture and mining).  However, the potential contribution of nature-based tourism to the economy and to poverty alleviation is yet unclear.  Further, little is known about barriers to achieving government targets and optimum management options for improving the sector&apos;s achievements.  Thus the Development Objective of the proposed project seeks the following outcome: More accurate information on nature-based tourism-lead economic growth and poverty potential leads Zambian decision-makers to initiate scaling up the investment in nature-based tourism as well as optimize management systems.  This project contributes to a larger set of studies embraced by a group of donors and partners under the umbrella of the Natural Resource Consultative Forum (NRCF).  The audience for this work is the Government, the NRCF, the PRSP Committee, Private Sector Associations, NGOs and donors.</narrative>
  </description>
